<!--
  MIASMA_NURSERY_KINDS_1 — juvenile-locked variants of the Grey Sea's nursery
  roster (design/Jawa/worldbuilding/biomes/the_miasma.md §4, R11: "the wild
  roster carries only the YOUNG side; the adult rides the Grey Sea/terminator
  sheets"). Owner ruling at the 2026-09-10 sitting: sea creatures raise their
  young in the Miasma.

  Mechanism, verified against Verse/PawnGenerator.cs and Verse/LifeStageUtility.cs
  before use (never guess a mechanism): PawnKindDef.maxGenerationAge is an int,
  years; these fish/crabs have an AnimalAdult threshold as low as 0.15 years
  (~2 months), which no integer can express, and forcing y<=0 against a
  continuous age-generation curve would fail its 300-try loop and spam
  Log.Error on every spawn. The real, working mechanism is
  LifeStageUtility.GetLifeStageAgeForYears: it returns the LAST entry in
  race.lifeStageAges whose minAge is below the rolled age, capped at the
  list's own length. Drop the AnimalAdult entry from lifeStageAges entirely
  and the pawn plateaus at Juvenile forever, at any rolled age: no
  maxGenerationAge needed. PawnKindDef.lifeStages is trimmed to match (2
  entries instead of 3), so it never reaches for the 3rd (full-adult) texture
  index. Same art, same tools/stats (inherited, unlisted fields stay
  inherited under ParentName Def-inheritance); only the life-stage ceiling
  changes. The Grey Sea/terminator roster keeps using the un-capped RSW_*
  defNames for adults (out of this item's scope: only the Miasma wildAnimals
  patch).
-->
<Defs>

  <ThingDef ParentName="RSW_Mee">
    <defName>RSW_MeeJuv</defName>
    <label>young mee scalefish</label>
    <description>A mee scalefish too young for the open sea, still schooling in the mangal shallows where it hatched. Small, quick, and almost charming -- and every scavenger who has fished a delta channel knows better than to wonder where its mother is.</description>
    <race>
      <lifeStageAges>
        <li>
          <def>AnimalBaby</def>
          <minAge>0</minAge>
        </li>
        <li>
          <def>AnimalJuvenile</def>
          <minAge>0.05</minAge>
        </li>
      </lifeStageAges>
    </race>
  </ThingDef>

